{
  "_readme": "Every monster in the game. Edit this file, then run Prince's Palace > Build Default Content in the Unity Editor to regenerate. Only id, displayName, and maxHealth are required — everything else is optional and gets a reasonable auto-derived default if left out (see EnemyEntryResolver.cs for the exact formulas). weakness/resistance are COMMA-SEPARATED LISTS of: Physical, Fire, Ice, Nature, Poison, Arcane (case-insensitive) — \"Fire\" and \"Fire, Ice\" are both valid, and an attack matching any listed weakness deals +50% damage while one matching any listed resistance deals -50%. Matching several weaknesses at once is impossible (an attack carries one type), so listing more elements widens what hurts a monster rather than deepening it. No element may appear in both lists. Leaving a field out derives a single element from the id; write \"none\" to say a monster genuinely has no weakness or no resistance. Set isBoss to true only for monsters that should appear exclusively in the dungeon's final room; a boss room draws from every boss whose minFloor it has reached, so which bosses a depth can field is decided entirely by this list — there is no separate per-biome boss table, and a boss is the only one at its depth exactly when it is the only entry that qualifies.",
